# Intentionally left unset here. Which value applies depends on who serves
# the UI, and the answer is different in the two deployment shapes:
#
#   Vercel (default, ./start_public.sh)
#     Vercel's own dashboard environment variable supplies VITE_API_BASE_URL,
#     and it must be the current Cloudflare tunnel URL. A real environment
#     variable wins over this file at build time, so leaving it unset here
#     keeps the dashboard as the single place it is set. The tunnel hostname
#     changes on every restart, so this needs updating and redeploying each
#     time; start_public.sh prints the exact value.
#
#   Local single-origin (./start_public.sh --local)
#     Unset, so src/services/api.ts falls back to '/api', which vite preview
#     proxies to the backend (vite.config.ts). One origin, no CORS, and
#     nothing to update when the tunnel URL changes.
#
# This previously pinned one specific trycloudflare.com hostname, which broke
# the moment that tunnel was restarted and was already dead when found.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
